q1. concatanate array with reverse:

here we have to create new array and paste the element from original array till n and after n just reverse using the indicies of original array.
new array size 2*n;
ans[i] = nums[i];
ans[i+n] =   nums[n-i-1]

eg1: I
nput: nums = [1,2,3]

Output: [1,2,3,3,2,1]

Explanation:

The first n elements of ans are the same as nums.

For the next n = 3 elements, each element is taken from nums in reverse order:

ans[3] = nums[2] = 3
ans[4] = nums[1] = 2
ans[5] = nums[0] = 1
Thus, ans = [1, 2, 3, 3, 2, 1].


class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> concatWithReverse(vector<int>& nums) {
        int n = nums.size();
        vector<int>ans(2*n);

        for(int i = 0 ; i<n ; i++){
            ans[i] = nums[i];
            ans[n+i] = nums[n-1-i];
        }




        return ans;
        
    }
};

